PXL
----

Minimal 2D graphics library in C99.

Features:
  - 2D primitives: line, rect, circle, triangle (outline + filled)
  - Canvas with scissor clipping, color, clear, blit
  - ARGB8888 pixel buffer (pixbuf)
  - Backends: SDL2, X11
  - Keyboard/mouse input

Build:
  make          # lib
  make lint     # run lint
  make test     # run tests
  make examples # demos
  make clean    # cleaning

  Backend selection via BACKEND=sdl or BACKEND=x11 (default)
  Changing Backends requires manual make clean.
  Test and demo will work only if main lib use the same BACKEND. Use make clean as needed.

Quick start:
    pxl_backend_init("Title", 800, 600, false);
    while (!pxl_input_is_pressed(PXL_WM_QUIT)) {
        pxl_backend_poll_events(&input);
        pxl_backend_begin_frame(&pb);
        pxl_canvas_init(&cnv, &pb);
        /* drawing: pxl_draw_*(), pxl_canvas_clear() */
        pxl_backend_end_frame();
    }
    backend_deinit();

Examples:
  - demo_sketch.c - Etch-a-Sketch: arrow/Vim keys for drawing, Shift for big steps,
                    ESC to clear, Q to quit
  - demo_pong.c   - Pong game: vim keys (J=down, K=up), simple predictive AI,
                    score display, FPS counter
  - demo_loops.c  - Game loop comparison: 3 squares on same line showing
                    Variable vs Fixed Accum vs Fixed Lerp timesteps
                    (1-4: slowdown factor, R: reset)
  - demo_gas.c    - Boltzmann gas simulation: spatial grid optimized particle collisions,
                    elastic physics, random colors
                    (Up/Down: add/remove 10 particles, ESC to quit)

Architecture:
  Core:
    buf.h         - ARGB8888 pixel buffer with stride alignment
    geom.h        - Geometry primitives (rect, span, point) and clipping
    canvas.h      - Drawing surface with color, scissor, clear, blit
    draw.h/c      - 2D primitives (line, rect, circle, triangle)
    err.h         - Error handling

  Backend:
    backend.h     - Backend interface (5 functions)
    input.h       - Input state handling (keyboard, mouse, window events)
    backend_sdl.c - SDL2 backend (uses SDL_PIXELFORMAT_ARGB8888)
    backend_x11.c - X11 backend (uses ARGB visual)

  Loop:
    stepper.h     - Time-stepped physics loop helper (fixed timestep, interpolation)

